cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite the archived release and the article."
title: "Locked paired validation of closed-loop therapy software: controller rankings are not robust to analysis choices"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Alizargar"
    given-names: "Javad"
    affiliation: "Department of Nursing, National Taipei University of Nursing and Health Sciences, Taipei, Taiwan"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2966-1315"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility package for a PeerJ Computer Science Research Article on the
  evaluation of delayed-feedback controllers for coupled photothermal-photodynamic
  simulation. The package contains the locked validation atlas, the frozen
  predicted-baseline-success scoring rule, a cluster-robust inference pipeline
  (bootstrap intervals, sign-flip permutation tests, Holm correction, minimum
  detectable effects), a specification curve, Pareto dominance and Dirichlet
  weight-sensitivity analyses, and the manuscript build.
keywords:
  - closed-loop control
  - therapy software
  - validation protocol
  - cluster bootstrap
  - permutation test
  - multiplicity correction
  - specification curve
  - Pareto analysis
  - reproducibility
  - photothermal-photodynamic simulation
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-28"
license: MIT
